## Context
Missing work the implementation review surfaced (panel/cycle2/
review-implementation.md §5.1): X5 gates the RFC on the segmenter's measured
precision, and seg/1 — line classification, heading candidates (numbering
patterns, case shape, headword rhythm: median gap and MAD over candidate
spacing), entry cut at accepted headings, confidence = fraction of text inside
confirmed entries, fallback below 0.5 to synthetic ~6k-token entries at
paragraph boundaries, labeled — has no implementation anywhere. Days of new
code standing between 0025's X5 and 0027, priced nowhere until now. Spec:
DESIGN.md §2.2. Political-review checkpoint applies: check zotero#6012's state
before building — structured extraction landing upstream makes heuristic
segmentation a fallback at best (panel/cycle2/review-political.md finding 5).

## Exit criteria
- [ ] #6012 checkpoint recorded here before implementation starts
- [ ] seg/1 runnable over flat /fulltext text, emitting entries + confidence
- [ ] deterministic on fixture text; identity string (seg/1) for the chunker key
- [ ] X5 (0025) can consume it on the author's machine
